AB  - Dyslexia, a learning disorder that affects children often goes unnoticed until it starts to have an impact, on their academic performance. It is important to identify and provide support for dyslexia at a stage. This study introduces a method for detecting using machine learning models. We used a set of cognitive features from a group of young learners as our dataset. Our study evaluated the performance of Machine Learning (ML) algorithms, including Artificial Neural Networks (ANNs) in distinguishing between profiles of individuals with dyslexia and those without. The results show levels of accuracy with our ANN based model achieving a good accuracy in early detection of dyslexia. Additionally, we discuss in this paper how the proposed model can be interpreted and its potential usefulness for specialists and educators.
