AB  - This research proposes the neural network (NN)-fuzzy logic control (FLC)-based methodology, which is designed with two stages of execution. Stage-1 is composed with the NN approach; it takes the input from the scanned image, the input from the classified clustered group, processes it with hidden layers, and generates the final output, which is input to the FLC in stage 2. The input of stage 2 converts the input into fuzzified data (0s and 1s) and trains the FLC system with fuzzified set values. The trained data has been simulated for further stages in the FLC-based decision-making approach and integrated to identify the character patterns based on the trained dataset. FLC-based planting and normalization techniques are integrated for re-training the data. The dataset has been framed with more than 6200 handwritten image characters, which were written by 235 writers. It aligned with the pre-processing, classification, and filtering stages and achieved a 99.8% recognition rate.
